35,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The delivery schedules show inspection fixes stay on time, but comfort projects slip a year. The diaries confirm six weeks lost to weather.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The timetable shows we paid for off-site space for two terms! The booking data says general rooms are always full, but specialist ones sit empty.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The freeze left grounds posts empty, yet technicians have spare hours. They also log hours on manual checks the equipment cannot handle.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The reviews show high satisfaction when any department could book the space. Surveys in older blocks found hazardous materials, adding months to openings.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The tender data confirms my fears. Mechanical plant costs jumped a fifth, and the audiovisual kit has no renewal reserve. The paper figures are a lie.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Mizuki, those hazardous materials explain the delays. I am glad we checked. @Benjamin, that cost jump is worrying.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Mizuki, that is great! High satisfaction when everyone can book it matches my data. @George, those spare technician hours are a real asset we should use!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I am not so sure. Those spare hours are already consumed by manual routines. Adding more work will break them.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, you are right. We cannot exploit their spare time. @Yumi, the booking data aligns with my review findings. General spaces perform best.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shizue, the weather delays are a nuisance, but the financial erosion is the real killer. @Yumi, general spaces are indeed the only ones with actual demand.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, I hear you. But for me, the calendar is the enemy. We must avoid anything exposed to the rain.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I agree! Indoor projects keep the timetable safe. @George, please help us find a plan that does not add to your team’s heavy load.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I appreciate the thought. But I will not let us bury the technicians under new duties. We must find a plan that respects their limits.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Yumi, I agree. We must respect George’s limits. @Shizue, indoor work avoids the weather risks you flagged. Let us focus on accessible, general spaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi"",""George"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, accessible spaces are wise, but I worry about the long-term maintenance costs. @George, we must ensure the plan does not require new equipment without a funded reserve.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki"",""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
