60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"I am so glad we are all here. The data points to indoor, general spaces. I worry about the calendar slipping, so I hope we choose wisely.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"I am excited to see the options! Candidate C, the Central Study Commons, looks perfect. It is indoor, general, and matches our booking data perfectly!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,Candidate D is a trap. It demands new equipment and more manual checks. I will not let us break the technicians further.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Candidate C aligns with my review data. High satisfaction comes from spaces any department can book. It is the logical choice for user value.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate D is a financial black hole. The ventilation upgrade triggers that twenty percent cost jump, and the new gear lacks a renewal reserve.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Yumi, I agree. Candidate C is indoor, so it avoids the weather delays I fear. It also fits the general-use pattern we all see.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Shizue, I am so happy we agree! Candidate C keeps the timetable safe and the rooms full. It is the best choice for everyone!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I am glad you see it. But the service desk in C adds to the daily load. We must ensure it does not become another burden for my team.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is a valid concern. We must ensure the service desk is staffed by existing library personnel, not your technicians. @Benjamin, C avoids the equipment trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, precisely. C is a conversion, not a new build. It avoids the mechanical plant inflation and the reserve trap. It is the only fiscally honest option here.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@George, I understand your worry. Let us ensure the desk is light. @Benjamin, I am relieved C avoids the cost traps. It feels like the right path.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@George, I completely understand! Let us promise that the desk will be minimal and handled by library staff, so your team stays safe.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, I appreciate the assurance. If the desk stays light, C is acceptable. I will not let my team carry the weight of this project.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shizue, I agree. C is the only option that respects the data and our people. I am ready to vote.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
